<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>The list is an Alpine <code>citedByFilter</code> (<code>treatment_list.js</code>). Every row carries its rank under each sort key, so sorting sets a CSS <code>order</code> and filtering toggles a class: the list is never rebuilt. The applied and recognized filter sections are a union: a row shows when either has a ticked tier. A chart cell, a meter tier or a Narrow by row narrows the list further, shown as a chip that names the narrowing and removes it.</p>
  <p>Rows with evidence are native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>: Enter or Space opens one.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>"N of M" is a polite live status, so filtering is announced. The filter menu is a <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> of native checkboxes that closes on Escape or a click outside (<code>sidebar_tree.js</code> handles both for every <code>details.list-filter</code>). Each row's rail colour repeats its first pill, never replaces it.</p></div>

